e,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(y^{2})\\,i+(- 2 x^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =((t^{3})^{2})\\,i+(- 2 (t^{4})^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(t^{6})\\,i+(- 2 t^{8})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r'(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{4})i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{3})j \\\\  & =(4 t^{3})\\,i+(3 t^{2})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =((t^{6})\\,i+(- 2 t^{8})\\,j)\\cdot ((4 t^{3})\\,i+(3 t^{2})\\,j) \\\\  & =(t^{6})\\cdot (4 t^{3})+(- 2 t^{8})\\cdot (3 t^{2}) \\\\  & =- 6 t^{10} + 4 t^{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F(r)\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{3}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{3}(- 6 t^{10} + 4 t^{9})\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560183 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10e2473a-7ecd-5c81-b672-db12be2f9d23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}(- \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560132} {:answer/id #uuid "66224a06-98ab-5fad-b9b5-5d4a40da649c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560161} {:answer/id #uuid "c4a93688-3a3e-5787-853b-25cb35330f67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}(- \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560200} {:answer/id #uuid "e43cfe1d-16f3-5772-8982-d15cb951335f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}(1)\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560210} {:answer/id #uuid "f10312fc-2eaf-5fdd-902f-4104757887fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}(-1)\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f10312fc-2eaf-5fdd-902f-4104757887fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}(-1)\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560214} :answer-field/id #uuid "69a19aea-9cac-5ffe-bb63-04acf1a5bd19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560164}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9cad2e1c-3fd7-5abc-a45f-1ba0aa4a145f" :question/problem "Which integral is obtained from $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(y)\\,i+(- x)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}]$? Use the supplied parameterization and limits to compute $F(r(t))\\cdot r'(t)$. Do not evaluate the integral or change variables." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=\\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,y=\\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(y)\\,i+(- x)\\,j \\\\  & =((\\sin{\\left(t \\right)}))\\,i+(- (\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}))\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r'(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\  & =(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =((\\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j)\\cdot ((- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j) \\\\  & =(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot (- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})+(- \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot (\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F(r)\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}(-1)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560194 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "347604a6-fc29-5235-a40e-c4b974503a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}(- 2 t^{7} + 12 t^{6})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560147} {:answer/id #uuid "692110f8-3f18-56d8-9db5-0decd985e753" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}(- 2 t^{7})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560163} {:answer/id #uuid "82ea29ed-ba48-5255-b7d8-4759e8f3c4ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}(12 t^{6})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560174} {:answer/id #uuid "b2e6ca92-0fd1-53cd-8e65-d7e4fa20bfa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}(- t^{6} + 4 t^{4})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560193} {:answer/id #uuid "d6dc348d-d61f-5310-b464-54dc51822d33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}(2 t^{7} - 12 t^{6})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "347604a6-fc29-5235-a40e-c4b974503a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}(- 2 t^{7} + 12 t^{6})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560147} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddd4e2de-caba-5381-9532-6515c5b57a7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b8acbc35-3fad-5a85-bfc1-6bd439a2af48" :question/problem "Which integral is obtained from $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(- y^{2})\\,i+(4 x^{2})\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t^{2})\\,i+(t^{3})\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2]$? Use the supplied parameterization and limits to compute $F(r(t))\\cdot r'(t)$. Do not evaluate the integral or change variables." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t^{2},\\,y=t^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(- y^{2})\\,i+(4 x^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(- (t^{3})^{2})\\,i+(4 (t^{2})^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(- t^{6})\\,i+(4 t^{4})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r'(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{2})i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{3})j \\\\  & =(2 t)\\,i+(3 t^{2})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =((- t^{6})\\,i+(4 t^{4})\\,j)\\cdot ((2 t)\\,i+(3 t^{2})\\,j) \\\\  & =(- t^{6})\\cdot (2 t)+(4 t^{4})\\cdot (3 t^{2}) \\\\  & =- 2 t^{7} + 12 t^{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F(r)\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{2}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{2}(- 2 t^{7} + 12 t^{6})\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68628931-5917-506d-9dff-cd9f8bbc7b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}}(- 2 t^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560162} {:answer/id #uuid "77c5a4f2-31fb-5985-a30d-d68bcda53ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}}(t^{2} \\left(- 2 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + t \\left(3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right))\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560169} {:answer/id #uuid "c6e171d8-646b-54e3-b47b-b2bf53c0c924" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}}(3 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 t \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560203} {:answer/id #uuid "efb092da-cb53-5fb2-878f-d365f984296f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}}(5 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560212} {:answer/id #uuid "fbbcde59-6af9-54b2-8c4d-996bd8287034" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}}(- t^{2} \\left(- 2 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) - t \\left(3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right))\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77c5a4f2-31fb-5985-a30d-d68bcda53ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}}(t^{2} \\left(- 2 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + t \\left(3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right))\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560169} :answer-field/id #uuid "db671629-2024-5c4e-95bd-d304c4e96f05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c300e91f-d29b-52cd-bc77-53bb950d5cac" :question/problem "Which integral is obtained from $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(x + 2 y)\\,i+(x + 3 y)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}]$? Use the supplied parameterization and limits to compute $F(r(t))\\cdot r'(t)$. Do not evaluate the integral or change variables." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,y=t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(x + 2 y)\\,i+(x + 3 y)\\,j \\\\  & =((t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) + 2 (t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}))\\,i+((t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) + 3 (t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}))\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r'(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\  & =(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =((2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(3 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j)\\cdot ((- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j) \\\\  & =(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot (- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})+(3 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot (t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\  & =(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot (- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})+(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot (- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot (t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})+(3 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot (t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\  & =- 2 t^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 t \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\  & =t^{2} \\left(- 2 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + t \\left(3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F(r)\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}}(t^{2} \\left(- 2 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + t \\left(3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right))\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560215 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dbb8114-0022-545b-b749-b3e641678284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}(t e^{2 t} + 1)\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560149} {:answer/id #uuid "5243f7e4-74ef-5df2-9100-845d622c7a72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}(- t e^{2 t} - 1)\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560153} {:answer/id #uuid "abe385ed-8d08-52ec-ae91-225fba4548b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}(2 \\sqrt{t} + t e^{t})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560190} {:answer/id #uuid "ba644c3a-40bf-59f7-9a07-a986b9585af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}(1)\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560196} {:answer/id #uuid "cdca2a95-175e-5c86-b898-ea1220da8ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}(t e^{2 t})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dbb8114-0022-545b-b749-b3e641678284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}(t e^{2 t} + 1)\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560149} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9f3daab-6a8a-5ae4-ada6-b16d6d099a72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f547fa50-e9ed-52ea-ac31-f84758ccc7ba" :question/problem "Which integral is obtained from $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(x y^{2})\\,i+(2 y)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(e^{t})\\,i+(\\sqrt{t})\\,j$ for $t\\in [1,3]$? Use the supplied parameterization and limits to compute $F(r(t))\\cdot r'(t)$. Do not evaluate the integral or change variables." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=e^{t},\\,y=\\sqrt{t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(x y^{2})\\,i+(2 y)\\,j \\\\  & =((e^{t}) (\\sqrt{t})^{2})\\,i+(2 (\\sqrt{t}))\\,j \\\\  & =(t e^{t})\\,i+(2 \\sqrt{t})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r'(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{t})i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})j \\\\  & =(e^{t})\\,i+\\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =((t e^{t})\\,i+(2 \\sqrt{t})\\,j)\\cdot ((e^{t})\\,i+\\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\,j) \\\\  & =(t e^{t})\\cdot (e^{t})+(2 \\sqrt{t})\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{t}}\\right) \\\\  & =t e^{2 t} + 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F(r)\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{1}^{3}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}(t e^{2 t} + 1)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560219 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17e89266-d4a1-5535-be58-9db6669fae57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}(- 4 t^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560134} {:answer/id #uuid "5979a1a7-83d7-5674-a4d7-e6cb418720b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}(7 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560154} {:answer/id #uuid "6015e95f-cad5-5129-8008-f13592f1a067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}(3 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 t \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560158} {:answer/id #uuid "62ab536d-0865-50cf-acb0-d3db8534033d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}(- t^{2} \\left(- 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) - t \\left(3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right))\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560159} {:answer/id #uuid "91227625-325d-5a82-a06d-d544ad1a411c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}(t^{2} \\left(- 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + t \\left(3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right))\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91227625-325d-5a82-a06d-d544ad1a411c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}(t^{2} \\left(- 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + t \\left(3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right))\\,dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560180} :answer-field/id #uuid "28b7a085-84f4-5355-b06f-113513cbca6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "fd911363-4a99-52e5-97ea-c6a788ed91ec" :question/problem "Which integral is obtained from $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(- 2 x + 4 y)\\,i+(2 x + 3 y)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi}{3}]$? Use the supplied parameterization and limits to compute $F(r(t))\\cdot r'(t)$. Do not evaluate the integral or change variables." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,y=t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(- 2 x + 4 y)\\,i+(2 x + 3 y)\\,j \\\\  & =(- 2 (t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) + 4 (t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}))\\,i+(2 (t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) + 3 (t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}))\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r'(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\  & =(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =((4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(3 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j)\\cdot ((- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j) \\\\  & =(4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot (- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})+(3 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot (t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\  & =(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot (- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})+(4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot (- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})+(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot (t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})+(3 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot (t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\  & =- 4 t^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 t \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\  & =t^{2} \\left(- 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + t \\left(3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F(r)\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}(t^{2} \\left(- 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + t \\left(3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right))\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567350 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37789fbf-187a-5931-87ee-f6efcb8d4882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567357} {:answer/id #uuid "406da1ca-1b0f-5a51-85fc-0d59b9f5c2b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567359} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb6d923-5c04-5b94-b393-aa363763c35c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567362} {:answer/id #uuid "84c3282d-d14b-5f40-af1f-205eaf8a9b65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\pi + 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567369} {:answer/id #uuid "9a94a97f-e8ac-51dc-b17b-778c4e14f24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37789fbf-187a-5931-87ee-f6efcb8d4882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567357} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dde938b-9bc6-56c2-8869-4846463cfa11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0809daf7-1c3a-50f9-b744-3b2f57eaa183" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(- 2 x)\\,i+(- 2 y + 2)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in[\\frac{\\pi}{2},2 \\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(- 2 x)\\,i+(- 2 y + 2)\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(- 2 \\left(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 2 \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + 2\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =(- 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- 6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j \\\\  & =(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left((- 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- 6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,j\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left((3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})+(- 6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- 18 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} +(18 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=- 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}(- 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\left[6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} \\\\  & =((6))-((0)) \\\\  & =(6)-(0) \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567354 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "067d7587-bd7a-55ca-b2a9-817044886453" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567349} {:answer/id #uuid "33f9719e-3e95-52b4-919a-e855b575c1c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567355} {:answer/id #uuid "5d9eb42f-0bfc-567b-a6cf-e1098750c4ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567363} {:answer/id #uuid "9147b4dd-04fe-5fd1-8299-b6061cdd5d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567373} {:answer/id #uuid "b5966bc5-1c82-5adb-b53d-5dcb7e743f51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33f9719e-3e95-52b4-919a-e855b575c1c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567355} :answer-field/id #uuid "632e0419-a120-5f91-b9be-603360314bbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "337254b1-2fa0-54a0-9d70-76189ce2de0c" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(x^{2} y)\\,i+(x + 1)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(2 t)\\,i+(t + 1)\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,1].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2 t,\\quad y=t + 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(x^{2} y)\\,i+(x + 1)\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(2 t\\right)^{2} \\left(t + 1\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(\\left(2 t\\right) + 1\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =(4 t^{2} \\left(t + 1\\right))\\,i+(2 t + 1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t + 1)\\,j \\\\  & =(2)\\,i+(1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\left((4 t^{2} \\left(t + 1\\right))\\,i+(2 t + 1)\\,j\\right)\\cdot\\left((2)\\,i+(1)\\,j\\right) \\\\ &=(4 t^{2} \\left(t + 1\\right))\\cdot(2)+(2 t + 1)\\cdot(1) \\\\ &=(8 t^{3} + 8 t^{2})+(2 t + 1) \\\\ &=8 t^{3} + 8 t^{2} + 2 t + 1\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}(8 t^{3} + 8 t^{2} + 2 t + 1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[2 t^{4} + \\frac{8 t^{3}}{3} + t^{2} + t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((1)+(1)+(2)+\\left(\\frac{8}{3}\\right))-((0)+(0)+(0)+(0)) \\\\ &=\\left(\\frac{20}{3}\\right)-(0) \\\\ &=\\frac{20}{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567356 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09f959b2-0ffe-576b-9e02-b7396da8770a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30 - \\frac{15 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567351} {:answer/id #uuid "76ba4b8e-08a9-5d7d-acec-c1ba3fa23731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567366} {:answer/id #uuid "8758f828-2dc9-5477-aa58-2e3270158b19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567370} {:answer/id #uuid "c75678bd-5ef0-563a-a7a9-134f15b2947f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567377} {:answer/id #uuid "d941523f-47c5-5e3a-8409-70777fef6ecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d941523f-47c5-5e3a-8409-70777fef6ecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567380} :answer-field/id #uuid "9820ad9d-0462-5026-b84e-b4ae332e6b83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "360cbd2a-7568-5a87-84ac-a04c5046eb33" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(5 x)\\,i+(5 y - 5)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in[\\frac{\\pi}{2},2 \\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(5 x)\\,i+(5 y - 5)\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(5 \\left(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(5 \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) - 5\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =(15 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(15 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 5)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j \\\\  & =(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left((15 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(15 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 5)\\,j\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left((3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(15 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})+(15 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 5) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(45 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} +(- 45 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 15 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=15 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}(15 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\left[- 15 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} \\\\  & =((-15))-((0)) \\\\  & =(-15)-(0) \\\\  & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567365 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c6c388f-6945-5085-a52f-1550351c42c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\left(-7\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567353} {:answer/id #uuid "8e57943f-170c-50e6-b5b2-adf2146e2c68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\left(9\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567372} {:answer/id #uuid "cc47fc32-7150-505d-bbc7-14230ad6a69f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\left(-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567378} {:answer/id #uuid "d20656cd-722a-5245-b740-acf463570a82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\left(2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567379} {:answer/id #uuid "f78fa774-904e-5be7-a83f-6cd598799e95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\left(-11\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c6c388f-6945-5085-a52f-1550351c42c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\left(-7\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567353} :answer-field/id #uuid "16fa1355-c929-5c19-8a01-ccbc29477515" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "759e78d6-7a3c-53d5-83ac-8b0533a5e4b8" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$ given that $$\n\\displaystyle F(x,y)=(-5)\\left(\\frac{y+1}{x}\\,i-\\frac{2(x-1)}{y}\\,j\\right)\n$$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+(t-1)\\,j$ for $t\\in [3,4].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx={t}^{2},\\,y=t-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(-5)\\left(\\frac{y+1}{x}\\,i-\\frac{2(x-1)}{y}\\,j\\right) \\\\  & =(-5)\\left(\\frac{(t-1)+1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i-\\frac{2({t}^{2}-1)}{t-1}\\,j\\right) \\\\  & =(-5)\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\,i-2(t+1)\\,j\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(-5)\\left((\\frac{1}{t}\\,i-2(t+1)\\,j)\\right)\\cdot (2t\\,i+j) \\\\ &=(-5)\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot 2t-2(t+1)\\cdot 1\\right) \\\\ &=(-5)\\left(2-2(t+1)\\cdot 1\\right) \\\\ &=(-5)\\left(-2t\\right).\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-5)\\left({\\int }_{3}^{4}(-2t)\\,dt\\right) \\\\  & =(-5)\\left({[-{t}^{2}]}_{3}^{4}\\right) \\\\  & =(-5)\\left([-16+9]\\right) \\\\  & =(-5)\\left(-7\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567368 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dc4ce1e-eafd-5783-9383-568f1601d09b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\left(-4-\\sqrt{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567358} {:answer/id #uuid "4bec57b6-4b6a-5921-a981-9e3f449068b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\left(-2+\\sqrt{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567361} {:answer/id #uuid "8a03e0c2-20dc-5c9e-aa85-b421c94b43e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\left(\\sqrt{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567371} {:answer/id #uuid "de8a8253-5270-5081-8567-22d741f3d493" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\left(1-\\sqrt{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567381} {:answer/id #uuid "f955c89d-840b-5d78-8735-84aef633daff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\left(2-\\sqrt{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f955c89d-840b-5d78-8735-84aef633daff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\left(2-\\sqrt{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567383} :answer-field/id #uuid "4702667f-3b1e-5bd1-81e7-1a8c1903dba7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "825d8f89-9569-5641-b2e2-7d7b47441607" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(-1)\\left((y\\operatorname{\\sin}x)\\,i+(x+y)\\,j\\right)$ and $C$ is the path  $r(t)=\\operatorname{arcsin}t\\,i+2j$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{1}{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}t,\\,y=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(-1)\\left(2\\operatorname{\\sin}(\\operatorname{arcsin}t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{arcsin}t+2)\\,j\\right) \\\\ &=(-1)\\left(2t\\,i+(\\operatorname{arcsin}t+2)\\,j\\right).\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arcsin}t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(-1)\\left((2t\\,i+(\\operatorname{arcsin}t+2)\\,j)\\right)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\,i) \\\\ &=(-1)\\left(\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\right).\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-1)\\left({\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\,dt\\right) \\\\  & =(-1)\\left(-2\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}\\,{|}_{0}^{1/2}\\right) \\\\  & =(-1)\\left(-2(\\sqrt{1-{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{2}}-1)\\right) \\\\  & =(-1)\\left(2-\\sqrt{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567610 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28ce15f5-0bb2-5b9f-8592-4a0322f57984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567613} {:answer/id #uuid "6be5a42d-48ad-579e-8464-15b20cb13bf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567624} {:answer/id #uuid "7174f11b-5236-5b17-80e0-c3f1c474a3f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567625} {:answer/id #uuid "9ee59bb7-0247-5ce2-94b7-78c7a6934ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567631} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a33bd9-a584-5350-8006-b88aec66f376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6be5a42d-48ad-579e-8464-15b20cb13bf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567624} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4dd6b1e-2d1f-55b3-bc0f-ae10a6f9338d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567634}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0c1cffe4-89e3-539c-8366-f9f730b0b5bf" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y,z)=\\left(- 2 y z\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 2 x z\\right)\\,j+\\left(- 2 x y\\right)\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\left(t\\right)\\,i+\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1]$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t,\\qquad y=t^{2},\\qquad z=t^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =- 2 y z\\,i+- 2 x z\\,j+- 2 x y\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(- 2 \\left(t^{2}\\right) \\left(t^{3}\\right)\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 \\left(t\\right) \\left(t^{3}\\right)\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 \\left(t\\right) \\left(t^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =- 2 t^{5}\\,i+- 2 t^{4}\\,j+- 2 t^{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\,i+2 t\\,j+3 t^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(- 2 t^{5}\\right)\\left(1\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 t^{4}\\right)\\left(2 t\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 t^{3}\\right)\\left(3 t^{2}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- 2 t^{5}\\right)+\\left(- 4 t^{5}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 6 t^{5}\\right) \\\\ & =- 12 t^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- 12 t^{5}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[- 2 t^{6}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(- 2 \\left(1\\right)^{6}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(- 2 \\left(0\\right)^{6}\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(-2\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567619 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07c3725e-c0c2-5264-836b-29da1e78105e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567608} {:answer/id #uuid "3902e07f-4288-5939-b2ab-30b04c23f72e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567615} {:answer/id #uuid "442afe00-979a-56dd-b0bc-309c821b1c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567617} {:answer/id #uuid "8183c895-778f-535e-a306-bbe3f68a031f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{256}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567626} {:answer/id #uuid "d9276e20-a02a-565e-820e-49512f9082a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{248}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07c3725e-c0c2-5264-836b-29da1e78105e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567608} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bf57375-1445-5745-b9ed-baa2a3ba9179" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5085fef4-7fd0-53eb-86d0-cf3ca417cef0" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y,z)=\\left(x + z\\right)\\,i+\\left(- y + z\\right)\\,j+\\left(z^{2}\\right)\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\left(- 3 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\left(- 2 t\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,2]$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=- 3 t^{2},\\qquad y=t^{2},\\qquad z=- 2 t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\left(x + z\\right)\\,i+\\left(- y + z\\right)\\,j+z^{2}\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(\\left(- 3 t^{2}\\right) + \\left(- 2 t\\right)\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- \\left(t^{2}\\right) + \\left(- 2 t\\right)\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(\\left(- 2 t\\right)^{2}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =t \\left(- 3 t - 2\\right)\\,i+t \\left(- t - 2\\right)\\,j+4 t^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- 3 t^{2}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- 2 t\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =- 6 t\\,i+2 t\\,j+-2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(t \\left(- 3 t - 2\\right)\\right)\\left(- 6 t\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(t \\left(- t - 2\\right)\\right)\\left(2 t\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 t^{2}\\right)\\left(-2\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(12 t^{2}\\right)+\\left(18 t^{3}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 4 t^{2}\\right)+\\left(- 2 t^{3}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 8 t^{2}\\right) \\\\ & =16 t^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{2}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(16 t^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[4 t^{4}\\right]_{0}^{2} \\\\ & =\\left(4 \\left(2\\right)^{4}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(4 \\left(0\\right)^{4}\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(64\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567622 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19118b4b-4bc2-5c88-8d85-83c7961e1254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 - 8 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567612} {:answer/id #uuid "3c981510-d372-514a-ba17-bf1ad4b8a84d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 - 8 e^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567616} {:answer/id #uuid "869a09e2-29f3-501b-8d46-a3a351303d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 - 4 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567627} {:answer/id #uuid "8f114952-7b3d-5083-9495-4e6a3d63ab57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 - 8 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567628} {:answer/id #uuid "d35c70f3-b511-5406-8095-a9ea87fd3b05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 - 4 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "869a09e2-29f3-501b-8d46-a3a351303d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 - 4 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567627} :answer-field/id #uuid "64d003d1-5dd7-519b-8e96-10188b2bb175" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "614e802d-40e8-5229-a70d-76c0aae224ea" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y,z)=\\left(- 2 x\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 2 z\\right)\\,j+\\left(- 2 y\\right)\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 e^{2 t}\\right)\\,j+\\left(e^{- 2 t}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1]$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=2 e^{t},\\qquad y=3 e^{2 t},\\qquad z=e^{- 2 t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =- 2 x\\,i+- 2 z\\,j+- 2 y\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(- 2 \\left(2 e^{t}\\right)\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 \\left(e^{- 2 t}\\right)\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 \\left(3 e^{2 t}\\right)\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =- 4 e^{t}\\,i+- 2 e^{- 2 t}\\,j+- 6 e^{2 t}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(3 e^{2 t}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(e^{- 2 t}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =2 e^{t}\\,i+6 e^{2 t}\\,j+- 2 e^{- 2 t}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(- 4 e^{t}\\right)\\left(2 e^{t}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 e^{- 2 t}\\right)\\left(6 e^{2 t}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 6 e^{2 t}\\right)\\left(- 2 e^{- 2 t}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- 8 e^{2 t}\\right)+\\left(-12\\right)+\\left(12\\right) \\\\ & =- 8 e^{2 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- 8 e^{2 t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[- 4 e^{2 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(- 4 e^{2 \\left(1\\right)}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(- 4 e^{2 \\left(0\\right)}\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- 4 e^{2}\\right)+\\left(4\\right) \\\\ & =4 - 4 e^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567641 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b3aea38-b87a-56dd-8ce4-503d865b6f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 e - 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567614} {:answer/id #uuid "48e24e23-19cd-5b1e-961f-87233449e703" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567618} {:answer/id #uuid "c03ec57a-9fe2-5a90-b06b-a6efa1186cfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567633} {:answer/id #uuid "c4e584dd-d948-53ac-a204-a221a913fe62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 e^{2} - 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567635} {:answer/id #uuid "cabe9f8c-6ee6-5b11-be51-7f09ff277712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 e - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c03ec57a-9fe2-5a90-b06b-a6efa1186cfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567633} :answer-field/id #uuid "99161df0-4567-5c99-a438-db2731dac859" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ee017037-ec25-59e8-8e01-7de9481a9db8" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r\n$$ given that $$\n\\displaystyle F(x,y,z)=\\left(- \\frac{3 z}{x}\\right)\\,i+\\left(- \\frac{3 z}{y}\\right)\\,j+\\left(-3\\right)\\,k\n$$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\left(e^{t}\\right)\\,i+\\left(e^{t}\\right)\\,j+\\left(t\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1]$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=e^{t},\\qquad y=e^{t},\\qquad z=t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =- \\frac{3 z}{x}\\,i+- \\frac{3 z}{y}\\,j+-3\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(- \\frac{3 \\left(t\\right)}{\\left(e^{t}\\right)}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- \\frac{3 \\left(t\\right)}{\\left(e^{t}\\right)}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-3\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =- 3 t e^{- t}\\,i+- 3 t e^{- t}\\,j+-3\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(e^{t}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(e^{t}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =e^{t}\\,i+e^{t}\\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(- 3 t e^{- t}\\right)\\left(e^{t}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 3 t e^{- t}\\right)\\left(e^{t}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-3\\right)\\left(1\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- 3 t\\right)+\\left(- 3 t\\right)+\\left(-3\\right) \\\\ & =- 6 t - 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- 6 t - 3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[- 3 t^{2} - 3 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(- 3 \\left(1\\right)^{2} - 3 \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(- 3 \\left(0\\right)^{2} - 3 \\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(-6\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567642 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "187b0814-ff32-5e53-8e7f-2662b84ab3ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 + 2 e^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567611} {:answer/id #uuid "5f646a42-d955-534e-ac7a-7eba91309464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4 e^{3}}{3} + \\frac{1}{3 e^{3}} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567621} {:answer/id #uuid "931666ec-70e9-546b-a3b5-1ef5701b53b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8 + 2 e^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567629} {:answer/id #uuid "d7528caa-39a7-5128-8670-30b663eea2cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567638} {:answer/id #uuid "dcee7dff-3186-5635-b892-3f51c08f759c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2 + 2 e^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcee7dff-3186-5635-b892-3f51c08f759c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2 + 2 e^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567640} :answer-field/id #uuid "53663adc-e46e-50a2-bc6e-bbced3aa0324" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567620}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "fbfa162e-7011-59ff-b7df-d730808c6923" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y,z)=\\left(y\\right)\\,i+\\left(x\\right)\\,j+\\left(z\\right)\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\left(- e^{- 3 t}\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 2 e^{3 t}\\right)\\,j+\\left(- 2 e^{3 t}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1]$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=- e^{- 3 t},\\qquad y=- 2 e^{3 t},\\qquad z=- 2 e^{3 t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =y\\,i+x\\,j+z\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(\\left(- 2 e^{3 t}\\right)\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(\\left(- e^{- 3 t}\\right)\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(\\left(- 2 e^{3 t}\\right)\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =- 2 e^{3 t}\\,i+- e^{- 3 t}\\,j+- 2 e^{3 t}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- e^{- 3 t}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- 2 e^{3 t}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- 2 e^{3 t}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =3 e^{- 3 t}\\,i+- 6 e^{3 t}\\,j+- 6 e^{3 t}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(- 2 e^{3 t}\\right)\\left(3 e^{- 3 t}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- e^{- 3 t}\\right)\\left(- 6 e^{3 t}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 e^{3 t}\\right)\\left(- 6 e^{3 t}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(-6\\right)+\\left(6\\right)+\\left(12 e^{6 t}\\right) \\\\ & =12 e^{6 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(12 e^{6 t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[2 e^{6 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(2 e^{6 \\left(1\\right)}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(2 e^{6 \\left(0\\right)}\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(2 e^{6}\\right)+\\left(-2\\right) \\\\ & =-2 + 2 e^{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711713 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d8bbc97-aee7-51d5-a133-62f51f9489d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711714} {:answer/id #uuid "3731eb81-c2ef-5ad6-8c65-18e7386f58ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac\\pi2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711717} {:answer/id #uuid "5169f893-6e2b-579b-9c00-cfc40967b1fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac\\pi2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711718} {:answer/id #uuid "9dbca83f-456b-524a-b6bd-7ac92a6c8a5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711722} {:answer/id #uuid "b26dae46-00d3-5e40-a78d-ff640f8328e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3731eb81-c2ef-5ad6-8c65-18e7386f58ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac\\pi2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711717} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ee710f8-ba9c-5dc4-9bd9-a4334891732a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1129c3c2-8035-555f-8741-73e78e4cc223" :question/problem "Evaluate\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r,\n$$\nwhere $\\mathbf F(x,y)=y\\,\\mathbf i-x\\,\\mathbf j$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf r(t)=\\sin t\\,\\mathbf i+\\cos t\\,\\mathbf j$ for $0\\le t\\le\\frac\\pi2$." :question/worked-solution "Use\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n=\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\nAlong the path, $x=\\sin t$ and $y=\\cos t$, so\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))=\\cos t\\,\\mathbf i-\\sin t\\,\\mathbf j.\n$$\nDifferentiate the supplied path:\n$$\n\\mathbf r'(t)=\\cos t\\,\\mathbf i-\\sin t\\,\\mathbf j.\n$$\nThen\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\n&=\\cos^2t+(-\\sin t)(-\\sin t)\\\\\n&=\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t=1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n=\\int_0^{\\pi/2}1\\,\\mathrm dt\n=\\left[t\\right]_0^{\\pi/2}=\\frac\\pi2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711719 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "371f8358-fa99-5be1-81d4-9c3a0e9c4d5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}+\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711716} {:answer/id #uuid "6c82d25c-21a7-52f1-b9c3-a44aa4beea0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}-\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711720} {:answer/id #uuid "b60d756f-615f-5961-adf0-4c8382195801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi^2+\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711725} {:answer/id #uuid "c4ea4fbe-47ad-512f-b024-a377a71dd1f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711727} {:answer/id #uuid "c7e02e42-f612-53fd-99f4-1d78a5ae32c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "371f8358-fa99-5be1-81d4-9c3a0e9c4d5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}+\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711716} :answer-field/id #uuid "754efe93-295b-561d-8662-bcad696fd3bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6bf0d7bf-cb75-5497-944d-ce9561ee4d19" :question/problem "Evaluate\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r,\n$$\nwhere $\\mathbf F(x,y)=x\\,\\mathbf i+(y-1)\\,\\mathbf j$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf r(t)=t\\sin t\\,\\mathbf i+t\\cos t\\,\\mathbf j$ for $0\\le t\\le\\pi$." :question/worked-solution "Use the parametrized line-integral formula:\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n=\\int_0^\\pi\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\nSubstitute $x=t\\sin t$ and $y=t\\cos t$:\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\n=t\\sin t\\,\\mathbf i+(t\\cos t-1)\\,\\mathbf j.\n$$\nBoth coordinates require the product rule:\n$$\n\\mathbf r'(t)=(\\sin t+t\\cos t)\\,\\mathbf i\n+(\\cos t-t\\sin t)\\,\\mathbf j.\n$$\nTake the dot product and expand:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\n&=t\\sin t(\\sin t+t\\cos t)\\\\\n&\\quad +(t\\cos t-1)(\\cos t-t\\sin t)\\\\\n&=t\\sin^2t+t^2\\sin t\\cos t\\\\\n&\\quad +t\\cos^2t-t^2\\sin t\\cos t\\\\\n&\\quad -\\cos t+t\\sin t\\\\\n&=t-\\cos t+t\\sin t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe mixed terms cancel, but the offset in the field leaves two extra terms. To integrate them, note that\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}(-t\\cos t)=-\\cos t+t\\sin t.\n$$\nThus\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n&=\\int_0^\\pi(t-\\cos t+t\\sin t)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{t^2}{2}-t\\cos t\\right]_0^\\pi\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}-\\pi(-1)-0\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}+\\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711731 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c6f668c-17e0-550c-bf01-07a12e658a2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711711} {:answer/id #uuid "242cea8a-d0d6-5ff9-9db9-609f69774db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711715} {:answer/id #uuid "a2bb4c6b-fa10-5de9-b170-dacdd38a93fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711723} {:answer/id #uuid "b899e334-7875-55b2-b64e-9bf5bc3fd58a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711726} {:answer/id #uuid "e56381ff-011f-5196-bb9e-db008932bf3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2bb4c6b-fa10-5de9-b170-dacdd38a93fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711723} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcec324f-3af8-569f-b853-9e9716a7a80e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ea656ca1-5eae-5f73-9742-a04c3fb0299d" :question/problem "Evaluate\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r,\n$$\nwhere $\\mathbf F(x,y)=y\\,\\mathbf i+(x+y)\\,\\mathbf j$ and $C$ is given by $\\mathbf r(t)=(1+2t)\\,\\mathbf i+(2-t)\\,\\mathbf j$ for $0\\le t\\le1$.\n\n*Hint: Use*\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n=\\int_0^1\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\\,\\mathrm dt,\n\\qquad \\mathbf r'(t)=2\\,\\mathbf i-\\mathbf j.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Along the path, $x=1+2t$ and $y=2-t$. Substitute both coordinates into the field:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\n&=(2-t)\\,\\mathbf i+((1+2t)+(2-t))\\,\\mathbf j\\\\\n&=(2-t)\\,\\mathbf i+(3+t)\\,\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nDifferentiating the path gives $\\mathbf r'(t)=2\\,\\mathbf i-\\mathbf j$. Take the dot product, keeping the negative sign of the second tangent component:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\n&=2(2-t)-(3+t)\\\\\n&=1-3t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nNow evaluate the definite integral:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n&=\\int_0^1(1-3t)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[t-\\frac32t^2\\right]_0^1\\\\\n&=1-\\frac32=-\\frac12.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712197 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e8005cd-d522-518e-94f1-c3efac87f5f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712200} {:answer/id #uuid "5f45032a-58e0-5e2a-8a04-7734cee71830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712205} {:answer/id #uuid "7d2ccaa3-8520-5bce-ace6-cd316f7ca852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712206} {:answer/id #uuid "8f3e6dd8-8a81-5379-b79b-6e97469d2bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712208} {:answer/id #uuid "bcfccde5-1e0e-594b-9dec-7c3c841b1b6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d2ccaa3-8520-5bce-ace6-cd316f7ca852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712206} :answer-field/id #uuid "392d7d45-4b02-5ff8-afaa-d41bff58cc22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712204}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "037e8887-9c3a-5f11-9e31-adc1ce58051d" :question/problem "Evaluate\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r,\n$$\nwhere $\\mathbf F(x,y,z)=x\\,\\mathbf i+z\\,\\mathbf j+y\\,\\mathbf k$ and $C$ is the path\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=-\\sin t\\,\\mathbf i+\\sec t\\,\\mathbf j+\\cos t\\,\\mathbf k,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le\\frac\\pi4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_0^{\\pi/4}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\nAlong the curve, $x=-\\sin t$, $y=\\sec t$, and $z=\\cos t$. Therefore\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))=-\\sin t\\,\\mathbf i+\\cos t\\,\\mathbf j+\\sec t\\,\\mathbf k.\n$$\nDifferentiate each curve component, keeping both negative signs:\n$$\n\\mathbf r'(t)=-\\cos t\\,\\mathbf i+\\sec t\\tan t\\,\\mathbf j-\\sin t\\,\\mathbf k.\n$$\nTake the dot product before integrating:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)&=(-\\sin t)(-\\cos t)\\\\\n&\\quad+\\cos t\\sec t\\tan t-\\sec t\\sin t\\\\\n&=\\sin t\\cos t+\\tan t-\\tan t\\\\\n&=\\sin t\\cos t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe second and third terms cancel since $\\cos t\\sec t=1$ and $\\sec t\\sin t=\\tan t$. Finally,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_0^{\\pi/4}\\sin t\\cos t\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac12\\sin^2t\\right]_0^{\\pi/4}\\\\\n&=\\frac12\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\right)^2-0=\\frac14.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712207 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15d1bd99-62a6-5e78-bece-6beebe3d1a8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712202} {:answer/id #uuid "35dcc429-c1f5-5034-8ae8-49edd9151335" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{59}{60}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712203} {:answer/id #uuid "902a532c-4a7c-5365-8f98-3befb6b0e3b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712209} {:answer/id #uuid "a9592bd8-0bea-5d63-8e8d-f3445dcb2d7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712213} {:answer/id #uuid "da9fc589-a52b-5110-af96-8e1b148ff5e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{89}{60}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da9fc589-a52b-5110-af96-8e1b148ff5e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{89}{60}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712216} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e5fb502-0106-5c72-8d46-a125ea3adc64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8115f68b-3cd0-56ce-8bc0-c46dd4579a17" :question/problem "Evaluate\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r,\n$$\nwhere $\\mathbf F(x,y,z)=y\\,\\mathbf i+z\\,\\mathbf j+x\\,\\mathbf k$ and $C$ is the path\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=t\\,\\mathbf i+t^2\\,\\mathbf j+t^3\\,\\mathbf k,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_0^1\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\nAlong the curve, $x=t$, $y=t^2$, and $z=t^3$. Hence\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))=t^2\\,\\mathbf i+t^3\\,\\mathbf j+t\\,\\mathbf k.\n$$\nDifferentiating the curve gives\n$$\n\\mathbf r'(t)=\\mathbf i+2t\\,\\mathbf j+3t^2\\,\\mathbf k.\n$$\nMatch corresponding vector components in the dot product:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)&=t^2\\cdot1+t^3\\cdot2t+t\\cdot3t^2\\\\\n&=t^2+2t^4+3t^3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThus\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_0^1(t^2+2t^4+3t^3)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{t^3}{3}+\\frac{2t^5}{5}+\\frac{3t^4}{4}\\right]_0^1\\\\\n&=\\frac13+\\frac25+\\frac34=\\frac{89}{60}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712210 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0688cdf6-d31c-5f3d-8ef7-09531c5e4919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712198} {:answer/id #uuid "9c44e3ab-0930-5e73-aeb6-2017452f30c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712211} {:answer/id #uuid "a92412cc-5852-52f1-8137-c440b59d1109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712212} {:answer/id #uuid "cb7589d1-76f4-549f-943b-20beab280aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712215} {:answer/id #uuid "fb860bab-ba5f-5751-b983-ae98c29b4f51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb7589d1-76f4-549f-943b-20beab280aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712215} :answer-field/id #uuid "12bb06b8-131f-5b81-8dbf-727e3d8f3cc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712201}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "945843d3-8c25-5968-964d-9f9a2542a12d" :question/problem "Evaluate\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r,\n$$\nwhere $\\mathbf F(x,y,z)=x\\,\\mathbf i+z\\,\\mathbf j+y\\,\\mathbf k$ and\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=t\\,\\mathbf i+2t\\,\\mathbf j+(1-t)\\,\\mathbf k,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n$$\n*Hint: Use $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_0^1\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\\,\\mathrm dt$ with $\\mathbf r'(t)=\\mathbf i+2\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k$.*" :question/worked-solution "Use the parametrized line-integral formula:\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_0^1\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\nAlong the curve, $x=t$, $y=2t$, and $z=1-t$. Substitute these coordinates into the corresponding field components:\n$$\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))=t\\,\\mathbf i+(1-t)\\,\\mathbf j+2t\\,\\mathbf k.\n$$\nDifferentiate the curve component by component:\n$$\n\\mathbf r'(t)=\\mathbf i+2\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k.\n$$\nThe dot product includes the negative third component:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)&=t\\cdot1+(1-t)\\cdot2+2t\\cdot(-1)\\\\\n&=2-3t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nFinally,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_0^1(2-3t)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\\n&=\\left[2t-\\frac32t^2\\right]_0^1\\\\\n&=2-\\frac32=\\frac12.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30173ae3-8e67-51ee-8f89-6d95e51d48f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712371} {:answer/id #uuid "4a8af6c3-3974-551e-86c5-54fae030a860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{39}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712375} {:answer/id #uuid "6a176c1e-75bb-5e7b-9fc7-a3eff06746aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712379} {:answer/id #uuid "786bf17a-0e1a-5dcd-9358-c27d37d5dae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712382} {:answer/id #uuid "d9ebf3b9-f2c5-5fbf-a6bb-dcc503a0fa0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "786bf17a-0e1a-5dcd-9358-c27d37d5dae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712382} :answer-field/id #uuid "b77e2fca-86f8-5a8b-908f-6953377a408c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0d7a881e-8d60-5bd0-b8bc-99254fd65d35" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(2 y - 1)\\,i+(2 x - y + 1)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(- 2 t - 2)\\,i+(- t - 1)\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,1].$\n\n*Hint:* Use $\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm d r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=- 2 t - 2,\\quad y=- t - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(2 y - 1)\\,i+(2 x - y + 1)\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(2 \\left(- t - 1\\right) - 1\\right)\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\left(2 \\left(- 2 t - 2\\right) - \\left(- t - 1\\right) + 1\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- 2 t - 3)\\,i+(- 3 t - 2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 2 t - 2)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t - 1)\\,j \\\\  & =(-2)\\,i+(-1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(- 2 t - 3)\\,i+(- 3 t - 2)\\,j}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(-2)\\,i+(-1)\\,j}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- 2 t - 3)\\cdot(-2)+(- 3 t - 2) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(-1)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\left({4 t + 6}\\right)+\\left({3 t + 2}\\right) \\\\ &=7 t + 8\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left({7 t + 8}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{\\frac{7 t^{2}}{2} + 8 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((8)+\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right))-((0)+(0)) \\\\ &=\\left(\\frac{23}{2}\\right)-(0) \\\\ &=\\frac{23}{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712374 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17632d48-0b54-592e-a841-a1a207465cb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712369} {:answer/id #uuid "7318685a-323a-5513-ac96-3dcba61f2139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712380} {:answer/id #uuid "b53a9d1c-a494-508d-9584-dc064df6b7cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712389} {:answer/id #uuid "b624ba7b-71a9-5226-9d1b-280c84468974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712390} {:answer/id #uuid "ba485208-6ed9-5a36-bcce-ecad72f4b48c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b53a9d1c-a494-508d-9584-dc064df6b7cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712389} :answer-field/id #uuid "76e64c52-0983-57fd-93c6-b5342a5a7984" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "43aa9df2-3303-53b3-a49e-7ba0e92cb9e8" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(- y)\\,i+(- x - 2)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t + 2)\\,i+(2 t + 1)\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,1].$\n\n*Hint:* Use $\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm d r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t + 2,\\quad y=2 t + 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(- y)\\,i+(- x - 2)\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(- \\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(- \\left(t + 2\\right) - 2\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =(- 2 t - 1)\\,i+(- t - 4)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t + 2)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t + 1)\\,j \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(- 2 t - 1)\\,i+(- t - 4)\\,j}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(1)\\,i+(2)\\,j}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- 2 t - 1)\\cdot(1)+(- t - 4)\\cdot(2) \\\\ &=\\left({- 2 t - 1}\\right)+\\left({- 2 t - 8}\\right) \\\\ &=- 4 t - 9\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left({- 4 t - 9}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{- 2 t^{2} - 9 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((-9)+(-2))-((0)+(0)) \\\\ &=(-11)-(0) \\\\ &=-11\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "438852ab-3dd5-582b-aa84-759aaf3b786a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712373} {:answer/id #uuid "56f069f9-f6b5-54de-bd9f-0b5958dfbe71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712376} {:answer/id #uuid "8545e4a7-9b79-5fe1-9107-f407f1642d6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712383} {:answer/id #uuid "bb261588-6384-5511-bb1c-25d550c083b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712394} {:answer/id #uuid "e408771b-bca0-56fa-ab5d-3c55ecaa9934" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e408771b-bca0-56fa-ab5d-3c55ecaa9934" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712399} :answer-field/id #uuid "869b80d6-b62c-5baa-a9c9-6ecb7efd3eff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5c3aca75-294e-5fea-b965-6baeaac7a8b2" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(- 2 y)\\,i+(- 2 x)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t - 2)\\,i+(2 t + 2)\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,1].$\n\n*Hint:* Use $\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm d r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t - 2,\\quad y=2 t + 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(- 2 y)\\,i+(- 2 x)\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(- 2 \\left(2 t + 2\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 2 \\left(t - 2\\right)\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =(- 4 t - 4)\\,i+(- 2 t + 4)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t - 2)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t + 2)\\,j \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(- 4 t - 4)\\,i+(- 2 t + 4)\\,j}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(1)\\,i+(2)\\,j}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- 4 t - 4)\\cdot(1)+(- 2 t + 4)\\cdot(2) \\\\ &=\\left({- 4 t - 4}\\right)+\\left({- 4 t + 8}\\right) \\\\ &=- 8 t + 4\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left({- 8 t + 4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{- 4 t^{2} + 4 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((-4)+(4))-((0)+(0)) \\\\ &=(0)-(0) \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712387 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ae63b8e-ae9a-5bb2-90e4-144b06291077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712370} {:answer/id #uuid "3a0dbb0f-eeef-595d-8c3e-69a77725ee44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712372} {:answer/id #uuid "5b80454d-bf9f-534a-b9a4-fc57252dcaae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712377} {:answer/id #uuid "932fb550-b045-5de4-b81e-757813772386" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712386} {:answer/id #uuid "c4e4b6a7-5b71-557b-b85c-170100c69e9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "932fb550-b045-5de4-b81e-757813772386" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712386} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba9bf6c8-2c06-5140-955b-faffabc9c80c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9f8c8036-de79-5449-a62b-4bda22066e3c" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(- y + 1)\\,i+(- x + 1)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(- t)\\,i+(- t - 1)\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,1].$\n\n*Hint:* Use $\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm d r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=- t,\\quad y=- t - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(- y + 1)\\,i+(- x + 1)\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(- \\left(- t - 1\\right) + 1\\right)\\,i+\\left(- \\left(- t\\right) + 1\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =(t + 2)\\,i+(t + 1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t - 1)\\,j \\\\  & =(-1)\\,i+(-1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(t + 2)\\,i+(t + 1)\\,j}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(-1)\\,i+(-1)\\,j}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(t + 2)\\cdot(-1)+(t + 1)\\cdot(-1) \\\\ &=\\left({- t - 2}\\right)+\\left({- t - 1}\\right) \\\\ &=- 2 t - 3\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left({- 2 t - 3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{- t^{2} - 3 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((-1)+(-3))-((0)+(0)) \\\\ &=(-4)-(0) \\\\ &=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712400 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13e447b5-faca-5a5f-9083-9792edef2df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712368} {:answer/id #uuid "8e39e322-43d4-5827-912a-972febce881b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712385} {:answer/id #uuid "a7554cc5-3148-54d7-8545-a60ecc25d725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712388} {:answer/id #uuid "d5219b2e-d7d5-540a-bc1e-6c6401c12803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712397} {:answer/id #uuid "fd7c5ab3-2069-56a6-b689-4f5982f840ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13e447b5-faca-5a5f-9083-9792edef2df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712368} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb789be4-5b0f-5cca-83ca-dfe527339637" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712395}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e8a56c7d-30ab-5d35-b00b-bf5e54fe584e" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(- 2 y + 2)\\,i+(- 2 x - 2)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t - 1)\\,i+(2 t - 1)\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,1].$\n\n*Hint:* Use $\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm d r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t - 1,\\quad y=2 t - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(- 2 y + 2)\\,i+(- 2 x - 2)\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(- 2 \\left(2 t - 1\\right) + 2\\right)\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\left(- 2 \\left(t - 1\\right) - 2\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- 4 t + 4)\\,i+(- 2 t)\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t - 1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t - 1)\\,j \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(- 4 t + 4)\\,i+(- 2 t)\\,j}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(1)\\,i+(2)\\,j}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- 4 t + 4)\\cdot(1)+(- 2 t)\\cdot(2) \\\\ &=\\left({- 4 t + 4}\\right)+\\left({- 4 t}\\right) \\\\ &=- 8 t + 4\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left({- 8 t + 4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{- 4 t^{2} + 4 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((-4)+(4))-((0)+(0)) \\\\ &=(0)-(0) \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712445 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f882330-5fa5-55e2-95d1-7e79678dc6eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 \\pi \\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712443} {:answer/id #uuid "5c534942-8fa9-52b6-a60c-efd5b29e0848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\pi \\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712449} {:answer/id #uuid "6e88684d-7b8d-5a90-8507-7fa6ed89917b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712450} {:answer/id #uuid "8aeb8921-8724-5198-978a-d76050baa356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712454} {:answer/id #uuid "970dacda-86cd-59dc-9dec-a98958efb7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\pi \\left(1 + 4 \\pi\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c534942-8fa9-52b6-a60c-efd5b29e0848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\pi \\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712449} :answer-field/id #uuid "9daf3be8-f67e-5de9-b5c9-f956b9ba588a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "483e4ae6-79d4-5247-8e94-b6fc63ccde3d" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(- 2 x + 1)\\,i+(- 2 y - 1)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,2 \\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(- 2 x + 1)\\,i+(- 2 y - 1)\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(- 2 \\left(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + 1\\right)\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\left(- 2 \\left(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) - 1\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} +(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 1) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} - 2 t \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} +\\left({\\begin{aligned}&2 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} - 2 t \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\left({\\begin{aligned}&t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{- t^{2} + t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right]_{0}^{2 \\pi} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&((- 4 \\pi^{2})+(0)+(- 2 \\pi)) \\\\ &{} -((0)+(0)+(0))\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- 4 \\pi^{2} - 2 \\pi)-(0) \\\\ &=- 2 \\pi \\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right)\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThe offset terms integrate by the reverse product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(- t^{2} + t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712453 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d48242b-6023-5db7-8d3a-eeecb6026126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi \\left(4 + 5 \\pi\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712442} {:answer/id #uuid "6e88f163-54a1-5d50-9758-c76af130019a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi \\left(\\pi + 4\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712451} {:answer/id #uuid "d3bb970f-214a-5e0c-9e0d-2f2a0c88e94d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + 6 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712461} {:answer/id #uuid "e2037cf7-ebea-5360-9d1d-cb3ea7e9f088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712464} {:answer/id #uuid "f5f9a9b7-eb83-56cd-b7b6-22fbbf7aac3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi \\left(- 5 \\pi - 4\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e88f163-54a1-5d50-9758-c76af130019a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi \\left(\\pi + 4\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712451} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cce83b1-f5e4-552f-8181-ec9a1b346cf5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "83d3c56a-8bde-57d4-8339-cfbeec8ae536" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(x + 1)\\,i+(y + 2)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in[\\pi,2 \\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(x + 1)\\,i+(y + 2)\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\left(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + 1\\right)\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\left(\\left(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + 2\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} +(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} +\\left({\\begin{aligned}&- t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} + t \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}\\left({\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{\\frac{t^{2}}{2} + t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right]_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&((2 \\pi^{2})+(0)+(4 \\pi)) \\\\ &{} -(\\left(\\frac{\\pi^{2}}{2}\\right)+(0)+(- 2 \\pi))\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(4 \\pi + 2 \\pi^{2})-(- 2 \\pi + \\frac{\\pi^{2}}{2}) \\\\ &=\\frac{3 \\pi \\left(\\pi + 4\\right)}{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThe offset terms integrate by the reverse product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(\\frac{t^{2}}{2} + t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712463 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21c60d00-9b09-5422-ad29-73cb2388f6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\pi \\left(-2 + \\pi\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712441} {:answer/id #uuid "3fbc11ad-ba0e-50f4-a146-480e3f613902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712444} {:answer/id #uuid "51619b82-99ba-5533-81dd-94de10a3c468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 \\pi - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712448} {:answer/id #uuid "7df4856f-c431-5056-9b88-a9efa4468f83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712452} {:answer/id #uuid "c295ba11-ac49-5b1e-b3b1-caab94b667cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\pi \\left(-2 + \\pi\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21c60d00-9b09-5422-ad29-73cb2388f6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\pi \\left(-2 + \\pi\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712441} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ef5e5c7-f47c-50f1-a460-e32ac79f1ac9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "de586386-7b1f-5d2e-a48c-3a3bc19f3b4f" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(2 x - 1)\\,i+(2 y - 2)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in[\\pi,2 \\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(2 x - 1)\\,i+(2 y - 2)\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(2 \\left(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) - 1\\right)\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\left(2 \\left(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) - 2\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2)\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 1) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} +(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&2 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} + 2 t \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} +\\left({\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} + 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} - 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t  \\\\ &{} - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}\\left({\\begin{aligned}&2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t  \\\\ &{} - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{t^{2} - t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right]_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&((4 \\pi^{2})+(0)+(- 4 \\pi)) \\\\ &{} -((\\pi^{2})+(0)+(2 \\pi))\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- 4 \\pi + 4 \\pi^{2})-(2 \\pi + \\pi^{2}) \\\\ &=3 \\pi \\left(-2 + \\pi\\right)\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThe offset terms integrate by the reverse product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(t^{2} - t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t  \\\\ &{} - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712465 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d34f86b-71a3-5f3b-a87d-b499775f5feb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 \\pi^{2} - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712440} {:answer/id #uuid "514f41cd-6266-5f8a-9dc4-f9ffe2f6fa3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712447} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e83f54-e849-594d-8929-7f7b5b427aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 \\pi^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712458} {:answer/id #uuid "c5675a16-3166-526a-be47-5e167558bd95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712460} {:answer/id #uuid "da681b53-3a27-5749-ab3b-8bf3dcad2440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 \\pi^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9e83f54-e849-594d-8929-7f7b5b427aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 \\pi^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712458} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fb08b1c-a405-5c9d-aafd-4b0c7581df71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ec707abf-6267-5e8a-ab61-e05c91f03ed9" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(- 2 x + 2)\\,i+(- 2 y)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in[\\pi,2 \\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(- 2 x + 2)\\,i+(- 2 y)\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(- 2 \\left(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + 2\\right)\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\left(- 2 \\left(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} +(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} - 2 t \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} +\\left({\\begin{aligned}&2 t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} - 2 t \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}\\left({2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{- t^{2} + 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right]_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi} \\\\ &=((- 4 \\pi^{2})+(0))-((- \\pi^{2})+(0)) \\\\ &=(- 4 \\pi^{2})-(- \\pi^{2}) \\\\ &=- 3 \\pi^{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThe offset terms integrate by the reverse product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(- t^{2} + 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712528 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "164d3436-02fc-58ec-ad98-395139cc15db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[t(\\cos t+\\sin t)(\\cos t+t\\sin t)\\\\&\\quad+t(\\cos t+2\\sin t)(\\sin t+t\\cos t)\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712523} {:answer/id #uuid "19fafab9-d222-5527-ae9f-4637bedc8041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[t(\\cos t+\\sin t)(\\sin t+t\\cos t)\\\\&\\quad+t(\\cos t+2\\sin t)(\\cos t-t\\sin t)\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712524} {:answer/id #uuid "5c6f04b0-0112-5a27-be84-302fd8b79fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[t(\\cos t+\\sin t)(\\cos t-t\\sin t)\\\\&\\quad+t(\\cos t+2\\sin t)(\\sin t-t\\cos t)\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712531} {:answer/id #uuid "70fe4683-4b99-5fbb-aa6a-ac68c7760763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[t(\\cos t+\\sin t)\\cos t\\\\&\\quad+t(\\cos t+2\\sin t)\\sin t\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712533} {:answer/id #uuid "e1afd290-81f5-5155-8f82-f2abab13401d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[t(\\cos t+\\sin t)(\\cos t-t\\sin t)\\\\&\\quad+t(\\cos t+2\\sin t)(\\sin t+t\\cos t)\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1afd290-81f5-5155-8f82-f2abab13401d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[t(\\cos t+\\sin t)(\\cos t-t\\sin t)\\\\&\\quad+t(\\cos t+2\\sin t)(\\sin t+t\\cos t)\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712541} :answer-field/id #uuid "470ec447-ed81-5044-845d-e06021b3dc5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712529}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "447e6e82-3ebd-54bd-8760-5d4d27f34b99" :question/problem "Which ordinary definite integral represents $\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(x+y)\\,i+(x+2y)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=t\\cos t\\,i+t\\sin t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,1]$?\n\nUse the supplied parameterization and limits. Select the integral whose integrand is $F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)$; do not evaluate it." :question/worked-solution "Use\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve, $x=t\\cos t$ and $y=t\\sin t$. Substitute into both mixed field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))&=(t\\cos t+t\\sin t)\\,i+(t\\cos t+2t\\sin t)\\,j\\\\&=t(\\cos t+\\sin t)\\,i+t(\\cos t+2\\sin t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEach path component needs the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t\\cos t)&=\\cos t-t\\sin t,\\\\\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t\\sin t)&=\\sin t+t\\cos t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\nr^{\\prime}(t)=(\\cos t-t\\sin t)\\,i+(\\sin t+t\\cos t)\\,j.\n$$\n\nMultiply matching components. Keep the two products factored:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)&=t(\\cos t+\\sin t)(\\cos t-t\\sin t)\\\\&\\quad+t(\\cos t+2\\sin t)(\\sin t+t\\cos t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r&=\\int_0^1\\bigl[t(\\cos t+\\sin t)(\\cos t-t\\sin t)\\\\&\\qquad+t(\\cos t+2\\sin t)(\\sin t+t\\cos t)\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNo antiderivative or further expansion is needed."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712535 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36ce88dc-8921-5c0c-b680-14c54c03502a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}(3t^4+3t^5-2t^6)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712525} {:answer/id #uuid "43621b54-d7d6-5bd2-a416-d1de62638438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}(t^2+t^3-t^5)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712527} {:answer/id #uuid "7ecb2fc7-b596-51bf-bd7f-ab20fff642ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}(2t^3+2t^4-3t^5)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712534} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2ba97d-e13b-5478-a560-7b784062a09a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}(2t^3+2t^4-3t^7)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712540} {:answer/id #uuid "e774a275-6075-5aca-ad96-976f5fbbd1ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}(2t^3+2t^4+3t^7)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc2ba97d-e13b-5478-a560-7b784062a09a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}(2t^3+2t^4-3t^7)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712540} :answer-field/id #uuid "370884ca-bc2d-545d-80e1-324ac00f63f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "91647911-097b-5f0a-b4e4-6d9a03848a20" :question/problem "Which ordinary definite integral represents $\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(x+y)\\,i-xy\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=t^2\\,i+t^3\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,1]$?\n\nUse the supplied parameterization and limits. Select the integral whose integrand is $F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)$; do not evaluate it." :question/worked-solution "Use\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=t^2$ and $y=t^3$ into both components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))&=(t^2+t^3)\\,i-(t^2)(t^3)\\,j\\\\&=(t^2+t^3)\\,i-t^5\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both path components:\n\n$$\nr^{\\prime}(t)=2t\\,i+3t^2\\,j.\n$$\n\nThe dot product includes both coordinate derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)&=(t^2+t^3)(2t)+(-t^5)(3t^2)\\\\&=2t^3+2t^4-3t^7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_{0}^{1}(2t^3+2t^4-3t^7)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712539 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "632c96a6-32a3-5a76-95ab-e02f54444d18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}(t^3-t^2)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712532} {:answer/id #uuid "9e0f1d5e-7117-5535-9792-1aa315d5d811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}(t^6+3t^4)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712536} {:answer/id #uuid "be4039f4-30bd-5b08-931c-561ad99bd8bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}(t^6-3t^2)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712537} {:answer/id #uuid "c40c51b1-4594-59d6-abd1-bd585bbc7cf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}(t^6-t^2)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712538} {:answer/id #uuid "e5023fa3-64bb-5161-9c6c-58f1cb85418d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}(t^6-3t^4)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5023fa3-64bb-5161-9c6c-58f1cb85418d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}(t^6-3t^4)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712542} :answer-field/id #uuid "521a2c38-a20a-52ca-af45-a740ef754d3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c82d9dd3-6e0b-5343-9d08-6711b97e50be" :question/problem "Which ordinary definite integral represents $\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=y^2\\,i-x^2\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=t\\,i+t^3\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,1]$?\n\nUse the supplied parameterization and limits. Select the integral whose integrand is $F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)$; do not evaluate it.\n\n*Hint: $r^{\\prime}(t)=i+3t^2\\,j$. Substitute the coordinates into the field, then take the dot product.*" :question/worked-solution "For a vector field, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve, $x=t$ and $y=t^3$, so\n\n$$\nF(r(t))=(t^3)^2\\,i-t^2\\,j=t^6\\,i-t^2\\,j.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the path gives\n\n$$\nr^{\\prime}(t)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}t}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}(t^3)}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j=i+3t^2\\,j.\n$$\n\nMultiply corresponding components and add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)&=t^6(1)+(-t^2)(3t^2)\\\\&=t^6-3t^4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the supplied parameter limits:\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_{0}^{1}(t^6-3t^4)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18dcc185-da79-53c6-a5f6-b36686887462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712571} {:answer/id #uuid "30605da9-f207-5cce-a677-a058fcfb46b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712574} {:answer/id #uuid "86103a31-c9cf-5765-bba1-8f6871d26741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712585} {:answer/id #uuid "9f0a8720-5299-54b7-9974-aa070cdf5b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712586} {:answer/id #uuid "e434105b-673f-581d-aa00-a5ce84480c11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18dcc185-da79-53c6-a5f6-b36686887462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712571} :answer-field/id #uuid "d858b970-81f4-5dec-82c5-00774cef2b96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "281dd2cc-334b-570c-b759-821f2cc5e6b7" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y,z)=\\left(- z\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 2 y\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 x\\right)\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\,i+\\left(1 - t\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 t\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1]$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=2 t + 1,\\qquad y=1 - t,\\qquad z=2 t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =- z\\,i+- 2 y\\,j+2 x\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(- \\left(2 t\\right)\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 \\left(1 - t\\right)\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 \\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =- 2 t\\,i+\\left(2 t - 2\\right)\\,j+\\left(4 t + 2\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(1 - t\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(2 t\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =2\\,i+-\\,j+2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(- 2 t\\right)\\left(2\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 t - 2\\right)\\left(-1\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 t + 2\\right)\\left(2\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- 4 t\\right)+\\left(2\\right)+\\left(- 2 t\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4\\right)+\\left(8 t\\right) \\\\ & =2 t + 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(2 t + 6\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[t^{2} + 6 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(\\left(1\\right)^{2} + 6 \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(\\left(0\\right)^{2} + 6 \\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(7\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712575 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cc58cc1-33fb-5810-a43a-3e663bda11e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712567} {:answer/id #uuid "0f2d0f10-ef8a-5a51-a521-ac4bab36ac11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712569} {:answer/id #uuid "18b58827-a7e8-5b86-9c15-641ba6c7e58d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712570} {:answer/id #uuid "54513911-beea-5733-aa23-49982f7482f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712578} {:answer/id #uuid "ca89b0bd-7ee1-5a79-91e3-b39f7c397b66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca89b0bd-7ee1-5a79-91e3-b39f7c397b66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712590} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa053add-fe8b-5d85-b4c5-5b1b68be3d7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "48975f1c-148c-5f1d-bb3c-f81c5fa3cf45" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y,z)=\\left(- 2 z\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 2 x\\right)\\,j+\\left(y\\right)\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\left(- t - 1\\right)\\,i+\\left(t - 1\\right)\\,j+\\left(- 2 t\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1]$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=- t - 1,\\qquad y=t - 1,\\qquad z=- 2 t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =- 2 z\\,i+- 2 x\\,j+y\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(- 2 \\left(- 2 t\\right)\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 \\left(- t - 1\\right)\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(\\left(t - 1\\right)\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =4 t\\,i+\\left(2 t + 2\\right)\\,j+\\left(t - 1\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- t - 1\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t - 1\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- 2 t\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =-\\,i+\\,j+-2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(4 t\\right)\\left(-1\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 t + 2\\right)\\left(1\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(t - 1\\right)\\left(-2\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- 4 t\\right)+\\left(2\\right)+\\left(2 t\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2\\right)+\\left(- 2 t\\right) \\\\ & =4 - 4 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(4 - 4 t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[- 2 t^{2} + 4 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(- 2 \\left(1\\right)^{2} + 4 \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(- 2 \\left(0\\right)^{2} + 4 \\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(2\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712582 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09a66bf2-f12f-5617-92c2-c0d73eff05e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712566} {:answer/id #uuid "1a31d390-237f-5a11-92b3-ef3a53c59f01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712572} {:answer/id #uuid "4e99a31e-c338-57d6-864d-732ecc1793d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712577} {:answer/id #uuid "5b0c7634-90a0-5c20-9e43-b066c0f40400" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712579} {:answer/id #uuid "eeeb18d6-e188-5461-97ae-7ddb57bdebb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e99a31e-c338-57d6-864d-732ecc1793d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712577} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd53c725-ca10-5ccc-a380-f73f19dc93d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "669ebe32-b712-5ba4-88d6-00b55e12fd89" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y,z)=\\left(2 z\\right)\\,i+\\left(2 x\\right)\\,j+\\left(y\\right)\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\left(t - 1\\right)\\,i+\\left(- t\\right)\\,j+\\left(1 - t\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1]$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t - 1,\\qquad y=- t,\\qquad z=1 - t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =2 z\\,i+2 x\\,j+y\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(2 \\left(1 - t\\right)\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 \\left(t - 1\\right)\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(\\left(- t\\right)\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(2 - 2 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(2 t - 2\\right)\\,j+- t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t - 1\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- t\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(1 - t\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\,i+-\\,j+-\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(2 - 2 t\\right)\\left(1\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 t - 2\\right)\\left(-1\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- t\\right)\\left(-1\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(2\\right)+\\left(- 2 t\\right)+\\left(2\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 t\\right)+\\left(t\\right) \\\\ & =4 - 3 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(4 - 3 t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[- \\frac{3 t^{2}}{2} + 4 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(- \\frac{3 \\left(1\\right)^{2}}{2} + 4 \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(- \\frac{3 \\left(0\\right)^{2}}{2} + 4 \\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712583 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0391f69c-f167-50b2-8108-e0a5ce9f56a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712565} {:answer/id #uuid "0e583ce2-6988-5eeb-9447-fbc10b02ed69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712568} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b407ad-671e-55bb-81d6-df26f9776724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712596} {:answer/id #uuid "fb2fccb6-ac2d-5c62-830f-0542a315a830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712598} {:answer/id #uuid "fe10f972-e36e-5a09-83bd-bf67cc6094af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6b407ad-671e-55bb-81d6-df26f9776724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712596} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fea34e7-6b8b-5c2f-9c32-8ad2253b6e2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6e9421ad-6493-555c-9206-6862149833f8" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y,z)=\\left(- x\\right)\\,i+\\left(z\\right)\\,j+\\left(- 2 y\\right)\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\,i+\\left(2 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1]$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=2 t + 1,\\qquad y=2 t,\\qquad z=2 t + 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =- x\\,i+z\\,j+- 2 y\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(- \\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(\\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 \\left(2 t\\right)\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(- 2 t - 1\\right)\\,i+\\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\,j+- 4 t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(2 t\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =2\\,i+2\\,j+2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(- 2 t - 1\\right)\\left(2\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\left(2\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 4 t\\right)\\left(2\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(-2\\right)+\\left(- 4 t\\right)+\\left(2\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 t\\right)+\\left(- 8 t\\right) \\\\ & =- 8 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- 8 t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[- 4 t^{2}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(- 4 \\left(1\\right)^{2}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(- 4 \\left(0\\right)^{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(-4\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712592 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4aa0071a-1891-5ad5-86cc-28776ad0deda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712576} {:answer/id #uuid "62427ed2-53ee-5e87-baf0-8a945a48add7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712581} {:answer/id #uuid "7a851acc-b9a3-5567-8009-29aeb21043dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712584} {:answer/id #uuid "c908c9cc-f3b7-59d5-8a21-e2d5d7989dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712588} {:answer/id #uuid "f4dfa71e-cff6-5971-a938-c7010801c174" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4aa0071a-1891-5ad5-86cc-28776ad0deda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712576} :answer-field/id #uuid "c921211c-67be-525a-a4c2-0e67dc99e5eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712589}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d9944bc5-4da4-5093-a853-de1344785396" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y,z)=\\left(2 z\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 2 x\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 y\\right)\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\left(- 2 t - 1\\right)\\,i+\\left(- t\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1]$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=- 2 t - 1,\\qquad y=- t,\\qquad z=2 t + 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =2 z\\,i+- 2 x\\,j+2 y\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(2 \\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 \\left(- 2 t - 1\\right)\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 \\left(- t\\right)\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(4 t + 2\\right)\\,i+\\left(4 t + 2\\right)\\,j+- 2 t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- 2 t - 1\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- t\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(2 t + 1\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =-2\\,i+-\\,j+2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(4 t + 2\\right)\\left(-2\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 t + 2\\right)\\left(-1\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 t\\right)\\left(2\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(-4\\right)+\\left(- 8 t\\right)+\\left(-2\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 4 t\\right)+\\left(- 4 t\\right) \\\\ & =- 16 t - 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- 16 t - 6\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[- 8 t^{2} - 6 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(- 8 \\left(1\\right)^{2} - 6 \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(- 8 \\left(0\\right)^{2} - 6 \\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(-14\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712601 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49c670d2-93a9-55c6-8483-1438f40ff7b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{31}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712606} {:answer/id #uuid "8f7c9a42-2e2e-57a4-9140-62f84a706018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{53}{60}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712612} {:answer/id #uuid "946ad836-deea-55fb-b81e-61a62024cba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{73}{60}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712615} {:answer/id #uuid "9c07fd18-47c4-5ac2-a98e-68edf459411a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{43}{60}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712616} {:answer/id #uuid "e84e6b1f-5a4a-5691-84f6-f55e8cddb0bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f7c9a42-2e2e-57a4-9140-62f84a706018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{53}{60}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712612} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7098412-86de-5e02-b7e2-ba1986ec94d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712622}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2b0757ea-76f0-5dd3-87b6-62a31fe8cdf1" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y,z)=\\left(2 y\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 2 z\\right)\\,j+\\left(- x\\right)\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\left(t\\right)\\,i+\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1]$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t,\\qquad y=t^{2},\\qquad z=t^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =2 y\\,i+- 2 z\\,j+- x\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(2 \\left(t^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 \\left(t^{3}\\right)\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- \\left(t\\right)\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =2 t^{2}\\,i+- 2 t^{3}\\,j+- t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\,i+2 t\\,j+3 t^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(2 t^{2}\\right)\\left(1\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 t^{3}\\right)\\left(2 t\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- t\\right)\\left(3 t^{2}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(2 t^{2}\\right)+\\left(- 4 t^{4}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 3 t^{3}\\right) \\\\ & =t^{2} \\left(- 4 t^{2} - 3 t + 2\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(t^{2} \\left(- 4 t^{2} - 3 t + 2\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[- \\frac{4 t^{5}}{5} - \\frac{3 t^{4}}{4} + \\frac{2 t^{3}}{3}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(- \\frac{4 \\left(1\\right)^{5}}{5} - \\frac{3 \\left(1\\right)^{4}}{4} + \\frac{2 \\left(1\\right)^{3}}{3}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(- \\frac{4 \\left(0\\right)^{5}}{5} - \\frac{3 \\left(0\\right)^{4}}{4} + \\frac{2 \\left(0\\right)^{3}}{3}\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- \\frac{53}{60}\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =- \\frac{53}{60}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712603 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6634f370-bc48-5598-98be-67f5f12ce5b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712608} {:answer/id #uuid "7b739e7e-867d-5ea4-ad41-94da1067be32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712610} {:answer/id #uuid "942d05c6-d1f6-51af-b148-6864f2801298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712614} {:answer/id #uuid "f63063ef-488d-565c-9ec0-3e456aa8f126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712627} {:answer/id #uuid "f79d9b07-15a8-5006-8d84-1c6bfe3138e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f63063ef-488d-565c-9ec0-3e456aa8f126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712627} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9ba0c72-2043-5523-8524-db37b6ad0b69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712625}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "39d7cf5e-f9a1-52dc-93f5-fb9693dd0ca9" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y,z)=\\left(x\\right)\\,i+\\left(z\\right)\\,j+\\left(- y\\right)\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\left(t\\right)\\,i+\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1]$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t,\\qquad y=t^{2},\\qquad z=t^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =x\\,i+z\\,j+- y\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(\\left(t\\right)\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- \\left(t^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =t\\,i+t^{3}\\,j+- t^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\,i+2 t\\,j+3 t^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(t\\right)\\left(1\\right)+\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\left(2 t\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- t^{2}\\right)\\left(3 t^{2}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(t\\right)+\\left(2 t^{4}\\right)+\\left(- 3 t^{4}\\right) \\\\ & =- t^{4} + t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(- t^{4} + t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[- \\frac{t^{5}}{5} + \\frac{t^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(- \\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{5}}{5} + \\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(- \\frac{\\left(0\\right)^{5}}{5} + \\frac{\\left(0\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{3}{10}\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{3}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712607 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc2140d5-6ced-592e-97b2-d44efc489e64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712617} {:answer/id #uuid "d4868530-8862-5f91-8c43-9e4c8a70b2b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{37}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712619} {:answer/id #uuid "e5628fe1-d2d6-55a1-9f96-1686ec820ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{47}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712620} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f71594-a5b2-54c0-99e7-aa643701dd6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712621} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ee9603-44fc-5b41-8d5b-3e1e3faa7a73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6f71594-a5b2-54c0-99e7-aa643701dd6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712621} :answer-field/id #uuid "82960f19-baa4-54e2-bb27-d17dac893f6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712611}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5199be22-14cd-5513-9c62-2039c00429f7" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y,z)=\\left(x\\right)\\,i+\\left(z\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 y\\right)\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\left(t\\right)\\,i+\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1]$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t,\\qquad y=t^{2},\\qquad z=t^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =x\\,i+z\\,j+2 y\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(\\left(t\\right)\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 \\left(t^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =t\\,i+t^{3}\\,j+2 t^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\,i+2 t\\,j+3 t^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(t\\right)\\left(1\\right)+\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\left(2 t\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 t^{2}\\right)\\left(3 t^{2}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(t\\right)+\\left(2 t^{4}\\right)+\\left(6 t^{4}\\right) \\\\ & =8 t^{4} + t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(8 t^{4} + t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[\\frac{8 t^{5}}{5} + \\frac{t^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{8 \\left(1\\right)^{5}}{5} + \\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(\\frac{8 \\left(0\\right)^{5}}{5} + \\frac{\\left(0\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{21}{10}\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{21}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712624 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eac98b4-9a99-5b98-83ad-3490cfdfe908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712604} {:answer/id #uuid "407b2926-bbf8-5610-8fee-dd2737bf009e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712605} {:answer/id #uuid "7542c75e-e9bd-5368-a89c-75b3cea63a23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{13}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712609} {:answer/id #uuid "93cded7c-52cd-5b96-ab70-426a1fce7ea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712613} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb553ca-f734-52d0-8f0f-544542030cba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7542c75e-e9bd-5368-a89c-75b3cea63a23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{13}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712609} :answer-field/id #uuid "327e76f3-c170-5093-8f06-bad63cf99150" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e92e891b-1514-5ae5-8180-f9d36aace7ff" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y,z)=\\left(- y\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 2 x\\right)\\,j+\\left(- z\\right)\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\left(t\\right)\\,i+\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1]$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t,\\qquad y=t^{2},\\qquad z=t^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =- y\\,i+- 2 x\\,j+- z\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(- \\left(t^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 \\left(t\\right)\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- \\left(t^{3}\\right)\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =- t^{2}\\,i+- 2 t\\,j+- t^{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\,i+2 t\\,j+3 t^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(- t^{2}\\right)\\left(1\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 t\\right)\\left(2 t\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- t^{3}\\right)\\left(3 t^{2}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- t^{2}\\right)+\\left(- 4 t^{2}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 3 t^{5}\\right) \\\\ & =t^{2} \\left(- 3 t^{3} - 5\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(t^{2} \\left(- 3 t^{3} - 5\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[- \\frac{t^{6}}{2} - \\frac{5 t^{3}}{3}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(- \\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{6}}{2} - \\frac{5 \\left(1\\right)^{3}}{3}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(- \\frac{\\left(0\\right)^{6}}{2} - \\frac{5 \\left(0\\right)^{3}}{3}\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- \\frac{13}{6}\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =- \\frac{13}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fae0589-765b-55b3-9c10-bb3cedb753cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713029} {:answer/id #uuid "7a1c1aa7-6c43-5b01-8a98-f7b440d6fdf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(1)\\\\&\\quad+(- \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713045} {:answer/id #uuid "941fa5bb-790c-5f9a-bde7-020ac9f8913c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713050} {:answer/id #uuid "9fce81d0-4b87-5c61-8823-ae1b222096aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713052} {:answer/id #uuid "abdef346-5072-5680-b0d0-0abd3f111b40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "941fa5bb-790c-5f9a-bde7-020ac9f8913c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713050} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d1aeb31-c2a8-567a-8be7-35087de69cd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "45dd7645-0290-5b22-93f8-95c9724e8a5f" :question/problem "Which ordinary definite integral represents $\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(y)\\,i+(- x)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2]$?\n\nUse the supplied parameterization and limits. Select the integral whose integrand is $F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)$; do not evaluate it.\n\n*Hint: $r^{\\prime}(t)=(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$. Substitute both coordinates into the field, then take the dot product.*" :question/worked-solution "Use the vector line-integral formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates $x=\\sin{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}$ into both field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))&=((\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}))\\,i\\\\&\\quad+(- (\\sin{\\left(t \\right)}))\\,j\\\\&=(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i\\\\&\\quad+(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each path component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)})=\\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\y^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})=- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply matching components and add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\\\&=(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the products using $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$ where applicable:\n\n$$\nF(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)=1.\n$$\n\nKeep the supplied parameter limits. The required integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713039 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d9db1f-bb91-557f-a268-db0a5a18e896" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{1}^{3}\\bigl[(2 e^{3 t})(1)\\\\&\\quad+(4 e^{t})(e^{t})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713031} {:answer/id #uuid "40943e93-6b05-57c1-ad6b-f6452d8dadb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{1}^{3}\\bigl[(- 2 \\sqrt{t} e^{2 t})(\\sqrt{t})\\\\&\\quad+(4 e^{t})(e^{t})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713033} {:answer/id #uuid "4c0e225b-2548-596f-9ba9-babde7c7ee2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{1}^{3}\\bigl[(2 \\sqrt{t} e^{2 t})(1)\\\\&\\quad+(4 e^{t})(e^{t})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713037} {:answer/id #uuid "627f2e57-c069-5ce4-8914-ec35c3745b71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{1}^{3}\\bigl[(2 \\sqrt{t} e^{2 t})\\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\\\&\\quad+(4 e^{t})(e^{t})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713041} {:answer/id #uuid "62c2fbac-2441-5234-9adf-dec35ee6ace9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{1}^{3}\\bigl[(2 e^{3 t})\\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\\\&\\quad+(4 e^{t})(e^{t})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "627f2e57-c069-5ce4-8914-ec35c3745b71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{1}^{3}\\bigl[(2 \\sqrt{t} e^{2 t})\\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\\\&\\quad+(4 e^{t})(e^{t})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713041} :answer-field/id #uuid "6360d371-92b7-5617-94ac-d2cd5c6b5e2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5d73125b-bb0a-593f-b95e-0c2ec21a36f9" :question/problem "Which ordinary definite integral represents $\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(2 x y^{2})\\,i+(4 y)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(\\sqrt{t})\\,i+(e^{t})\\,j$ for $t\\in [1,3]$?\n\nUse the supplied parameterization and limits. Select the integral whose integrand is $F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)$; do not evaluate it.\n\n*Hint: $r^{\\prime}(t)=\\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\,i+(e^{t})\\,j$. Substitute both coordinates into the field, then take the dot product.*" :question/worked-solution "Use the vector line-integral formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates $x=\\sqrt{t}$ and $y=e^{t}$ into both field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))&=(2 (\\sqrt{t}) (e^{t})^{2})\\,i\\\\&\\quad+(4 (e^{t}))\\,j\\\\&=(2 \\sqrt{t} e^{2 t})\\,i\\\\&\\quad+(4 e^{t})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each path component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})=\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{t}},\\\\y^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{t})=e^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply matching components and add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\\\&=(2 \\sqrt{t} e^{2 t})\\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\\\&\\quad+(4 e^{t})(e^{t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the products:\n\n$$\nF(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)=5 e^{2 t}.\n$$\n\nKeep the supplied parameter limits. The required integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{1}^{3}\\bigl[(2 \\sqrt{t} e^{2 t})\\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\\\&\\quad+(4 e^{t})(e^{t})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713049 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31a9217a-197e-5a79-b240-99e300064447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713030} {:answer/id #uuid "5ee5f34d-e213-57d2-bce5-67b0a900ab35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713040} {:answer/id #uuid "658a425c-c970-589c-918b-b176292d9f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(- t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713044} {:answer/id #uuid "838c8a44-1cae-5ecb-95b8-47a2aed2f55e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(- t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713046} {:answer/id #uuid "9445bfb2-13c3-5093-94ba-eb583e8a0dde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ee5f34d-e213-57d2-bce5-67b0a900ab35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713040} :answer-field/id #uuid "87248e49-49f7-578c-9410-6dc8605ae63a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713047}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8f8cf799-b912-5587-87a9-ee1b80067dc1" :question/problem "Which ordinary definite integral represents $\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(2 x)\\,i+(2 y)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,1]$?\n\nUse the supplied parameterization and limits. Select the integral whose integrand is $F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)$; do not evaluate it.\n\n*Hint: $r^{\\prime}(t)=(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$. Substitute both coordinates into the field, then take the dot product.*" :question/worked-solution "Use the vector line-integral formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates $x=t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}$ into both field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))&=(2 (t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}))\\,i\\\\&\\quad+(2 (t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}))\\,j\\\\&=(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i\\\\&\\quad+(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each path component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\y^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})=- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply matching components and add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\\\&=(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the products using $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$ where applicable:\n\n$$\nF(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)=2 t.\n$$\n\nKeep the supplied parameter limits. The required integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713053 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29480a7a-9779-5c72-aa5e-686ff4e445ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(t^{2})(1)\\\\&\\quad+(2 t^{2})(2 t)\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713027} {:answer/id #uuid "2ec826cf-d37f-51d6-b6f0-67fbd2fb728b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(t^{4})(1)\\\\&\\quad+(2 t^{2})(2 t)\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713028} {:answer/id #uuid "3f56a250-e546-53a1-85fc-56af3c1de3de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(t^{4})(1)\\\\&\\quad+(- 2 t^{2})(2 t)\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713032} {:answer/id #uuid "44144e91-61e3-5ba3-9647-17d13ebf94d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(t^{4})(1)\\\\&\\quad+(- 2 t^{2})(t^{2})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713034} {:answer/id #uuid "44df0283-ef1a-5749-bf7a-de86215aa9b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(t^{4})(1)\\\\&\\quad+(2 t^{2})(t^{2})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ec826cf-d37f-51d6-b6f0-67fbd2fb728b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(t^{4})(1)\\\\&\\quad+(2 t^{2})(2 t)\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713028} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc19804d-b831-52c7-be8a-47bb9f762af3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a3c6f36e-7d98-533f-bae0-60abf8216a47" :question/problem "Which ordinary definite integral represents $\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(y^{2})\\,i+(2 x^{2})\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t)\\,i+(t^{2})\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2]$?\n\nUse the supplied parameterization and limits. Select the integral whose integrand is $F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)$; do not evaluate it.\n\n*Hint: $r^{\\prime}(t)=(1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j$. Substitute both coordinates into the field, then take the dot product.*" :question/worked-solution "Use the vector line-integral formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates $x=t$ and $y=t^{2}$ into both field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))&=((t^{2})^{2})\\,i\\\\&\\quad+(2 (t)^{2})\\,j\\\\&=(t^{4})\\,i\\\\&\\quad+(2 t^{2})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each path component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t)=1,\\\\y^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{2})=2 t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply matching components and add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\\\&=(t^{4})(1)\\\\&\\quad+(2 t^{2})(2 t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the products:\n\n$$\nF(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)=t^{4} + 4 t^{3}.\n$$\n\nKeep the supplied parameter limits. The required integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(t^{4})(1)\\\\&\\quad+(2 t^{2})(2 t)\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713055 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ae17ad6-79a0-5742-ab49-d52fe47d5ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713048} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b3eabf-a12a-50fa-a39d-9353d982ea58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713056} {:answer/id #uuid "daf2b239-744f-57f7-b6b9-633285cdadb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[(2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(1)\\\\&\\quad+(- 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)(1)\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713058} {:answer/id #uuid "dcd7b501-3955-52d3-9685-eb3ced8dd2ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713059} {:answer/id #uuid "e2bf32ec-517d-582d-919f-f203d9ffebae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ae17ad6-79a0-5742-ab49-d52fe47d5ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713048} :answer-field/id #uuid "137b5e03-5115-58b0-ba79-05d93198ab61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713026}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "af26ebe9-3e62-557d-a2b8-0480b65b5604" :question/problem "Which ordinary definite integral represents $\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(- 2 x)\\,i+(- 2 y - 1)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,1]$?\n\nUse the supplied parameterization and limits. Select the integral whose integrand is $F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)$; do not evaluate it.\n\n*Hint: $r^{\\prime}(t)=(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$. Substitute both coordinates into the field, then take the dot product.*" :question/worked-solution "Use the vector line-integral formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates $x=\\sin{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}$ into both field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))&=(- 2 (\\sin{\\left(t \\right)}))\\,i\\\\&\\quad+(- 2 (\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) - 1)\\,j\\\\&=(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i\\\\&\\quad+(- 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each path component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)})=\\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\y^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})=- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply matching components and add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\\\&=(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the products using $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$ where applicable:\n\n$$\nF(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)=\\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nKeep the supplied parameter limits. The required integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1}\\bigl[(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 1)(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
